// The words of one presentation of a concept, from the pack. A concept carries
// its presentations as show_intuition, show_definition, show_example,
// show_non_example and show_worked lines (the last three may repeat). When there
// are several, the one sharing the most content words with the basis text is
// shown (plan_pick_overlap), and a rotating number picks among them when none
// shares any, so a learner who misses the same concept again sees a different
// instance. A worked example in mode "partial" is faded (fade.id). Answers ""
// when the concept has no text for that presentation.

plan_present_text(Pack plan_pack, int plan_concept_block, string plan_kind, string plan_mode, string plan_basis, int plan_rotate) {
  string[] plan_texts = pack_fields(plan_pack, plan_concept_block, "show_" + plan_kind);
  int plan_pick = plan_pick_overlap(plan_texts, plan_basis, plan_rotate);
  string plan_text_found = "";
} chain (Pack plan_pack, int plan_concept_block, string plan_kind, string plan_mode, string plan_basis, int plan_rotate) {
  if (plan_pick >= 0) {
    plan_text_found = plan_texts[plan_pick];
  }
  if (plan_pick >= 0 && plan_kind == "worked" && plan_mode == "partial") {
    plan_text_found = plan_fade(plan_text_found);
  }
} return string plan_text_found;
given pack_fixture_parse("concept: c\nshow_definition: D\nshow_example: alpha beta gamma\nshow_example: delta epsilon zeta\nshow_worked: assume x; then y, so z. Done.\nshow_non_example: n1\n") ((import pack_fixture_book), 0, "definition", "full", "", 0):("D")
